{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>If there are still many years.</b> There is no doubt that after the slave has remained in his master's house a long time, his labor becomes more valuable than it was at the start of his service. Therefore Scripture says that even though much time remains until the end of his sale-period, and there is no doubt that his labor has not yet reached the perfection it would have attained had he remained the entire time, nevertheless the redemption deducts from the sale price proportionately to the silver of his purchase — as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated: his silver is multiplied in two arrangements [of calculation] against the silver of his purchase (Kiddushin 20a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:06.608094403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}